# Patch: keep main-view core keymaps active
# Plugin: ravitemer/mcphub.nvim
# Tested against: 163b3ad [v6.2.0] with local patches 01-07 applied
#
# Problem: patch 05 added endpoint/agent row actions by deleting buffer-local
# keys (`e`, `t`, `d`, `a`, `A`, `r`, `R`, etc.) on every cursor move and only
# recreating them for endpoint/agent rows. On server, native server, tool,
# resource, and prompt rows, normal actions like `t` and `e` stopped working;
# `l` still worked because it was not deleted.
#
# Fix: keep core browse-mode keymaps registered and dispatch by the current row
# type. Endpoint and agent actions are row-aware silent mappings owned by the
# main view, so switching rows or views no longer deletes normal actions.

diff --git i/lua/mcphub/ui/views/main.lua w/lua/mcphub/ui/views/main.lua
--- i/lua/mcphub/ui/views/main.lua
+++ w/lua/mcphub/ui/views/main.lua
